lea-proxy refused %H: not in the egress allowlist. To allow it, run on the host: lea egress allow %H (applies live, no restart).
<html><body><p>lea-proxy refused %H: it is not in the egress allowlist. The user decides: on the host (never from inside lea), <code>lea egress allow %H</code> allows it and its subdomains at once, without restarting the proxy or any agent, and keeps it in ~/.config/lea/lea.conf; <code>lea egress deny %H</code> takes it back. The list is LEA_EGRESS_ALLOW in that file (comma separated; "default" keeps lea's default list, as in LEA_EGRESS_ALLOW="default,example.com").</p></body></html>
